2026-09-27T10:00:04.9970719Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9971339Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9972005Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9973137Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9974467Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9974588Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9974861Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9975274Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9975672Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9975800Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9976118Z ================
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9976287Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9976516Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9977081Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9977404Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9977572Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9977981Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9978232Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9978421Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9978988Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9979510Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9980623Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9981644Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9981831Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9982508Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9983399Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9983858Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9984347Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9985038Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:04.9985173Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0069810Z ========
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0070122Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0072470Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0074520Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0074871Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0075566Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0076755Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0077626Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0078442Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0079086Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0079733Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0079884Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0080248Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0080467Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0082393Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0084339Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0085348Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0086651Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:00:05.0086967Z 
